# This files feeds the disassembler with essential information.
# In this example of `apple1_hello` we indicate the range of the
# code and the table so disassembly will be perfect.
# A `*.map` file will tell you all the ranges you need. In case of 
# disassembling an unknown program, you can already put the list of
# ROM addresses and everything you know about it in this file and it
# will make the disassembly more fun.
# In other words: away with the garbage...
#
# A table that should not be handled as code, a known address that 
# will make it readable from the start. Imagine you put the 
# PIA/VIA/UART/TIM addresses and vectors here...

RANGE { start $0290; end $029D; type ByteTable; name "text"; };
LABEL { name "CharOut"; addr $FFEF; };
